From 8fde8094b697a4be0da62f7aa9d0bfa2a42ab026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mita5358 <kafitcohr@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:16:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/20] perf(dsh): fold the trajectory in slices so the first
 frame paints

Chat folds the session's whole event log into the trajectory build on every
render, and the first fold is unbounded. On the titan record that is 93k
events, nearly all of it assistant/message stream validation: 2.3 s of
main-thread work charged to the first frame, after the transcript was already
assembled.

Give extendTrajectory an optional budget and let Chat hand it 4k events per
tick. The build's source becomes a prefix of the snapshot and the next call
resumes through the same incremental path a live append uses, so nothing is
refolded and the ledger is identical once the fold catches up. The first
frame now paints before the fold starts; the strip and the trajectory scene
fill in over the following ticks.

Measured on the titan session in a mirror install: first visible content
16,518 ms -> 14,281 ms. verify-trace-projection gains a budget oracle (zero
budget, 3-event slices, partial prefix, oversized budget) and still passes
71/71 checks.
